read_named — resource-read tool mirror (DECIDED, planned)
=========================================================

status: DECIDED 2026-07-15, planned (wave TBD).
spec: "resource-read tool mirrors" under "mcp resources".
umbrella: plans/resource_tool_mirrors.

what it is: a builtin tool alias for the isabelle://named/{name}
resource — user-registered resources from the mcp_resource command
(named facts read at read time, diagnostic-command output, ML
generators). content is computed at read time, so dynamic fact
collections stay current.

advertised metadata (sketch)
----------------------------

name          read_named
description   "Read a user-registered named resource (from the
              mcp_resource command): a named fact collection,
              diagnostic-command output, or an ML generator, evaluated
              at read time. Same content as the isabelle://named/{name}
              resource."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["name"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}

backing: zero new mechanism — the same MCP_Resource read path
(MCP.read_resource, MCP_Session.ml_read_resource) the
isabelle://named/{name} read uses. one function, two surfaces.

note: read_named is a mirror of the READ; it does NOT enumerate the
named resources (that is resources/list, which lists named resources
concretely). if an autonomous mode also needs to DISCOVER named
resources without resources/list, that is a separate list-flavored
mirror — flag it in plans/resource_tool_mirrors if an eval shows the
need; not built now.

tests (sketch): [scala unit] row + dispatch + parity with the resource
read (over a registered demo resource, e.g. "greeting"); [e2e] read a
named resource by tool and by resource, byte-identical payloads.
